C     PDEV - MADLEN bridge from FOREX 4.12 PLOT() to the NITI frame.
C
C     FRAME CONTRACT (shared with dispak/dispak/extra.c, du_decode_stream):
C       word 0 = X in steps of 0.1 mm, octal integer
C       word 1 = Y in steps of 0.1 mm, octal integer
C       word 2 = pen state (0 = up, 1 = down)
C       words 3..63 = 0
C
C     PLOT() fills the 64-word COMMON /PDEVXY/ and passes FRAME(1) as the
C     only argument. On entry the accumulator holds the address of that
C     argument (FORTRAN-to-MADLEN calling convention, see
C     besm6.net/book/fortran-1976/03-madlen.md, section 46). MADLEN cannot
C     resolve FOREX COMMON symbols by name, so passing the address removes
C     the dependency on the linker layout of any particular deck.
C     ATI saves the address in R11; STX pops the saved accumulator to keep
C     the stack balanced; ITA reloads the address before each ЭК because
C     ЭК 01210 may clobber the accumulator. ЭК 01211 takes the frame address
C     from the accumulator. R11 needs no restoration (registers 8-12 and 14
C     are freely usable by an autocode subroutine).
 PDEV: ,NAME,PDEV
       1, VTM,
       ,ATI,11
       ,STX,
       ,ITA,11
       ,*50,1210B
       ,ITA,11
       ,*50,1211B
       13, UJ,
       ,END,
